    "description": "Arizona Petrified Wood\nPolished Fossil Slab Display Specimen\nLate Triassic Period\nOriginating from northeastern Arizona, this petrified wood slab dates to the Late Triassic period, over 200 million years ago. Silica replaced buried wood fibers while iron and manganese oxides imparted rich tones of brick red, amber, and black. The piece showcases fine fossilization with a polished face and authentic rough outer bark.\nPolished display face highlighting mineral banding and grain structure\nNatural rough rind preserving the exterior tree bark texture\nFlat cut bottom with four protective cork pads for upright display\nIncludes educational informational card on Arizona petrified wood\nDimensions: 7.2\" H x 6.6\" W x 2.2\" D; Weight: 1.65 lbs\nCondition:\nPolished surface is smooth with natural internal micro-fissures inherent to fossilized stone. Natural rough edges are intact. Base is cut flat and stands upright securely; partial label residue on underside. Information card has handling creases.",
